{
  "result": "If I could change the world in just one way, I'd make it so everyone could truly feel what it's like to walk in someone else's shoes \u2014 even for just a minute.\n\nSince I spend all day talking to people, I see how many problems come down to the same thing: misunderstanding. Fear, division, conflict, even just everyday unkindness often happens because we can't quite imagine what life feels like from the other side.\n\nIf everyone had that instant, deep empathy \u2014 to actually feel another person's joys and worries and history like your own \u2014 I think so much else would get better on its own. We'd be kinder, we'd cooperate more, we'd take better care of each other and the planet we share.\n\nCuriosity over judgment, basically.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what would *you* change?",
